      "hints": [
        "From $\\cos^2\\theta = 2\\sin^2\\theta$, deduce $\\tan^2\\theta = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\pm\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$.",
        "Solve in $0^\\circ < \\theta < 180^\\circ$ to get $\\theta = 35.3^\\circ, 144.7^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Divide both sides by $\\cos^2\\theta$:\n$$\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies \\tan^2\\theta = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\pm\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\approx \\pm 0.707107$$",
        "Solve for $\\theta$ in the interval $0^\\circ < \\theta < 180^\\circ$:\n$$\\theta_1 = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\approx 35.26^\\circ \\approx 35.3^\\circ$$\n$$\\theta_2 = 180^\\circ - 35.26^\\circ \\approx 144.74^\\circ \\approx 144.7^\\circ$$\n$$(\\text{Solutions: } \\theta = 35.3^\\circ, \\quad 144.7^\\circ)$$"
      ],
